<title>POLAND: OPTIMUS, MICROCOM FORM PARTNERSHIP.</title>
<headline>OPTIMUS, MICROCOM FORM PARTNERSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish computer maker Optimus SA and U.S. communications service firm Microcom Inc. signed an agreement under which Optimus would sell and distribute Microcom modems in Poland and neighbouring countries.</p>
<p>&quot;The agreement covers the period until the end of the year but has a clause that it could be extended for the next five years,&quot; Andrzej Zelek, Optimus deputy president, told a news conference after the signing on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Optimus president Roman Kluska, also present, said that his company hoped to win a 35-45 percent share of Poland's computer modem market. He would not say what was market share now.</p>
<p>Zelek said that Microcom modems would be built in Optimus' Prestige computer model and would be also available separately.</p>
<p>-- Barbara Wozniak +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
